# Project Memory Playbook

Use this playbook before project work that needs durable user preferences or project context.

- Sync and read `it-nanyuan/project-memory` before planning, designing, implementing, debugging, or reviewing.
- Apply recorded preferences and project conventions quietly in the work.
- Read design memory for UI, UX, visual, app, website, game, slide, or product-facing tasks.
- Update memory when the user expresses a durable like, dislike, correction, rule, or reusable project decision.
- Keep memory updates concise and commit them separately.
- Never store secrets, credentials, tokens, recovery details, temporary logs, or low-confidence guesses.
